Subject: [PATCH] nuttx: match the pinned Xtensa unsigned 16-bit wchar_t ABI

NuttX Xtensa takes wchar_t from the compiler's __WCHAR_TYPE__. The pinned
Espressif GCC 16.2.0 defines it as short unsigned int (16 bits), as checked
by the compiled native ABI witness. The architecture split in libc 0.2.191
omitted Xtensa; select the matching type explicitly. Native toolchains with
a different wchar_t model must fail the size/alignment/signedness ABI gate.

--- a/src/unix/nuttx/mod.rs
+++ b/src/unix/nuttx/mod.rs
@@ -39,3 +39,5 @@
 cfg_if! {
-    if #[cfg(any(target_arch = "riscv32", target_arch = "riscv64"))] {
+    if #[cfg(target_arch = "xtensa")] {
+        pub type wchar_t = c_ushort;
+    } else if #[cfg(any(target_arch = "riscv32", target_arch = "riscv64"))] {
         pub type wchar_t = c_int;
